{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00301",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.83,
      "end_seconds": 2.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Morning! Make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 3.45,
      "end_seconds": 7.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.03,
      "end_seconds": 10.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "So, have you been here before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.01,
      "end_seconds": 14.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "A couple of times, but not recently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.66,
      "end_seconds": 17.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Tell me what's been troubling you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 18.91,
      "end_seconds": 22.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "He's been having breathlessness when I lie flat, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.76,
      "end_seconds": 26.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.69,
      "end_seconds": 29.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "It's been going on for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.73,
      "end_seconds": 33.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Does it happen all the time or in spells?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.07,
      "end_seconds": 38.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Honestly, a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.69,
      "end_seconds": 42.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "What about tiredness, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.84,
      "end_seconds": 49.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Yes, for six months. I've also had swelling in both ankles, since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.58,
      "end_seconds": 55.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following. Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.54,
      "end_seconds": 61.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Uh, mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.52,
      "end_seconds": 66.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Okay, have you had any palpitations, calf pain or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.09,
      "end_seconds": 70.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.93,
      "end_seconds": 73.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Right, anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.62,
      "end_seconds": 75.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.56,
      "end_seconds": 78.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.54,
      "end_seconds": 90.29,
      "duration_seconds": 10.75,
      "text": "Not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.68,
      "end_seconds": 95.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.48,
      "end_seconds": 109.19,
      "duration_seconds": 12.71,
      "text": "I take ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure. I just want to get back to normal, really. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.72,
      "end_seconds": 113.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.05,
      "end_seconds": 114.89,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.13,
      "end_seconds": 125.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.02,
      "end_seconds": 135.81,
      "duration_seconds": 9.79,
      "text": "I had my appendix out about eight years ago. I've never really been one for hospitals. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.59,
      "end_seconds": 139.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "One moment, I'm updating your notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.39,
      "end_seconds": 159.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Good, where were we. How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.29,
      "end_seconds": 162.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "I smoke about ten cigarettes a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.93,
      "end_seconds": 165.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.14,
      "end_seconds": 170.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.89,
      "end_seconds": 176.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Just to be sure I've got this right, the ramipril, what dose was that again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.67,
      "end_seconds": 177.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.14,
      "text": "5 milligrams. Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.16,
      "end_seconds": 181.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.8,
      "end_seconds": 186.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Eggs. I come out in... well, stomach cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.9,
      "end_seconds": 190.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.06,
      "end_seconds": 193.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "My grandmother had breast cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.54,
      "end_seconds": 210.58,
      "duration_seconds": 16.04,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.66,
      "end_seconds": 213.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.93,
      "end_seconds": 217.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.82,
      "end_seconds": 221.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.13,
      "end_seconds": 236.69,
      "duration_seconds": 13.56,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.98,
      "end_seconds": 239.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.94,
      "end_seconds": 242.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.23,
      "end_seconds": 251.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.67,
      "end_seconds": 276.92,
      "duration_seconds": 16.25,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 89, blood pressure 127 over 75, temperature 37.0. Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.63,
      "end_seconds": 281.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.75,
      "end_seconds": 287.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with fluid overload related to the heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.17,
      "end_seconds": 289.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.99,
      "end_seconds": 308.98,
      "duration_seconds": 17.99,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like fluid overload related to the heart, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had breathlessness when you lie flat for about a month, and no calf pain or palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.36,
      "end_seconds": 312.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Exactly, uh, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.08,
      "end_seconds": 324.76,
      "duration_seconds": 11.68,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood tests for heart failure review. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's use furosemide, 40 milligrams, every morning, until we review. It's for fluid overload."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.94,
      "end_seconds": 327.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.45,
      "end_seconds": 350.03,
      "duration_seconds": 21.58,
      "text": "Keep the salt and the fluids moderate, no more than about one and a half litres a day. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. Please don't sit on it if the breathlessness gets worse or you can't lie down at all. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.41,
      "end_seconds": 352.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.76,
      "end_seconds": 357.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.42,
      "end_seconds": 362.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.24,
      "end_seconds": 370.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.81,
      "end_seconds": 379.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "So, I take the furosemide, 40 milligrams, every morning and come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.52,
      "end_seconds": 385.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. We're all set. Don't leave without asking if something's unclear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.7,
      "end_seconds": 388.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.08,
      "end_seconds": 389.82,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}